From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: a task dialog's "See details" is not cut to "See"

A task dialog's expando control ("See details" / "Hide details", for
expanded information) was laid out as wide as its text while it is drawn
with its arrow first: the text was cut to "See" and "Hide" in every task
dialog that has details -- File Explorer's Network Error among them. It is as
wide as the arrow and the text now.

Gate: test/taskexpando-gate.sh; mutant SG_MUTANT_EXPANDO_TEXT_ONLY.
---
--- a/dlls/comctl32/taskdialog.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/taskdialog.c
@@ -460,6 +460,12 @@
     max_text_height = DrawTextW(hdc, dialog_info->collapsed_text, -1, &rect, style);
     size->cy = max(size->cy, max_text_height);
     size->cx = max(size->cx, rect.right - rect.left);
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9662): the control is drawn with its arrow first, the text after it
+     * (taskdialog_draw_expando_control): it is as wide as both. It was as wide as the text alone,
+     * so "See details" showed as "See" and "Hide details" as "Hide". */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_EXPANDO_TEXT_ONLY
+    size->cx += icon_width + text_offset;
+#endif
     size->cx = min(size->cx, max_width);
 
     if (old_hfont) SelectObject(hdc, old_hfont);
